#: processes/kg/copy-into-folio.bpmn:28
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Taking an asset from an upstream knowledge graph into your own folio so you can edit it, comment on it or raise todos against it — without touching the upstream source and without losing where it came from. This is the fourth knowledge-graph affordance (`copy-into-folio` in `kg-affordances`). Like `copy-out-materialized.bpmn` for held library items, it is TWO WRITES AND A REFUSAL, gated up front by write capability: 1. Check whether the session holds a write capability (`git-push`, `github-api`, or `github-connector`). When none is available, degrade cleanly to read-only inspection (`browse`) and emit the `KgAsset` declaration snippet with `source` pre-filled rather than failing mid-procedure. 2. Read the asset and its origin (`instance`, `path`, `ref`) from the source knowledge graph without mutating the source. 3. Copy the asset into the target folio, declare it in the folio's `assets[]`, and stamp `KgAsset.source` (`{ instance, path, ref }` — `AssetSourceSchema` in `schemas/kg/kg-node.ts`). `source` absent means authored locally (a third state), so omitting `source` on a copy is the defect this process exists to prevent. 4. Verify the declared asset via `check:declaration-resolution` (`check:declared-assets`), then hand off to the folio author to edit, comment or raise todos on their copy."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/copy-into-folio.bpmn:149
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The copied asset is now writable content of the target folio with recorded upstream provenance (`KgAsset.source`). The folio author may edit it in place, attach review comments, or raise todos (`todo-manager`) against it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/copy-into-folio.bpmn:42
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The person adapting an upstream knowledge-graph asset in their own folio. Chooses which asset to copy and where it belongs, receives the read-only inspection when the session has no write capability, and edits, comments on or raises todos against the copy once it is stamped and verified."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/copy-into-folio.bpmn:68
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Triggered when a reader browsing a knowledge graph wants to take an asset into their own folio to edit it, annotate it or raise todos against it."
msgstr ""

